# Case: Independent Desktop role processes
# Mode: process
# Purpose: Normal runtime retains tray and service after GUI close and independently recreates GUI and quick-panel processes.
# Steps:
#   Start normal mode with explicit background intent, verify no initial GUI and a ready hidden panel, then open and close each UI role and verify cleanup.
#   Reject a GUI quit, retry the GUI-only restart, and request a full restart after saving a plugin change.
# Expected:
#   Tray, GUI, quick panel and unicd have independent process identities; tray activation works with unicd already running.
#   GUI-only restart returns the quit failure and preserves the tray, quick panel and unicd on retry. Full restart replaces the owned unicd and clears the pending configuration.
# Forbidden:
#   Resident hidden GUI, shared role PID, duplicate owners, foreign-profile activation, lost state, leaked processes, or native acceptance claims.

acceptance startup desktop-processes
